The Black's Law Dictionary (5th Edition) defines the word "show" as- to make apparent or clear by the evidence, to prove;
"deemed" as- to hold, consider, adjudge, believe, condemn, determine, construed as if true; "presume" as- to believe or accept on probable evidence; and "Presumption",
in Black's, "is a rule of law, statutory or judicial, by which finding of a basic fact gives rise to existence of presumed fact, until presumption is rebutted."
